## LOAD (binding)
8 cores shared with other projects' seats (load1 23.67 at 14:44, a long peak). Heavy = `npm ci`, any jest run, the neighbours, the verify. **Start a heavy job only while `uptime` load1 is below 7 at two reads 4 s apart** (not independent: say so), recorded beside the result; at or over, poll every 20-30 s, log each wait, do light work meanwhile (C1, C2, C3 polls, instrument writing, source reading, C6 by source, C10). One heavy job of yours at a time, never beside another seat's jest process you can see (the lock is for that). A MOVING heartbeat (counter plus `date`) to `session-tools/b897/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job; three unmoved beats = stuck: say so. A wait loop never uses `pgrep -f` on a pattern in its own command line (wait on a recorded pid with `kill -0`, or a done-marker file). Every command gets its input or none (`/dev/null`). NO artificial load. Budget (write at Step 0, about 50 tickets): two `npm ci`, base x2, gate whole x4, J alone x2, probe copy x2, 15 mutants, T0 x3, T1-T4, neighbours x2, one verify, one final run if the merge ref moved, plus other seats' tickets ahead in the FIFO (G198's verify first, likely). **If jest is not startable (load at or above 7 for 60 minutes), do the light work and report CONDITIONAL with "jest UNMEASURED"; never claim a cell result you did not run.**

